# Step 26: the Linux sandbox, in cortex-sandbox, and what it added to
# cortex-core, cortex-policy and cortex-cli.
#
# Each rule the sandbox enforces is broken here: what a command may write,
# the network filter, failing closed, the state a session reports, the
# levels that need the sandbox, the temporary directory, the protected
# paths, and what the model is told.

[break] write-root-widened-to-its-parent
rule: A command may write only under the write roots, not beside them.
file: crates/cortex-sandbox/src/confine.rs
in: landlock
find: created = grant(created, root, handled, abi)?;
replace: created = grant(created, root.parent().unwrap_or(root), handled, abi)?;
# The backends are built only with cortex-core beside it.
packages: cortex-sandbox, cortex-core
caught-by:
    cortex-sandbox::it confined::sys_the_workspace_and_the_temporary_directory_are_writable_and_nothing_else

[break] network-filter-not-loaded
